<title>USA: Howell to sell unit, cut debt.</title>
<headline>Howell to sell unit, cut debt.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Howell Corp said on Thursday that it entered a tentative deal to sell its research and reference fuels and chemical customer manufacturing business to Timberwilde Capital Group LLC for $20 million.</p>
<p>The deal has a potential for additional performance payments over the next five years and brings Howell out of the downstream processing and chemical industry, Howell said.</p>
<p>Howell, which plans to eliminate its $100 million debt from this deal and other asset sales, said it will focus on oil and gas asset growth to boost shareholder value.</p>
</text>
